    {
      "title": "Asian Paints Q2FY27 result: Profit rises 7.5% to ₹1,068 cr, sales grow 17%",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/asian-paints-q2fy27-result-profit-rises-7-5-to-1-068-cr-sales-grow-17-126102900944_1.html",
      "description": "Asian Paints Ltd on Thursday reported a 7.5 per cent year-on-year increase in consolidated net profit at Rs 1,067.6 crore for the September quarter, as strong sales growth across domestic coatings and international markets was partly offset by rising raw material costs and pressure on operating margins.\nConsolidated net sales rose 16.9 per cent to Rs 9,953.9 crore in the quarter ended September 30, while profit before depreciation, interest, tax and other income (PBDIT) increased 3.6 per cent to Rs 1,557.1 crore, the country's largest paintmaker said in a statement.\nThe PBDIT margin contracted to 15.6 per cent from 17.7 per cent a year earlier, reflecting the impact of sharp raw material inflation and supply constraints linked to geopolitical disruptions. The company said it absorbed part of the cost increases to protect consumer demand while implementing calibrated price hikes.\nThe board declared an interim dividend of Rs 5.75 per share, equivalent to 575 per cent of the face ...",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-29T10:21:50"
    },
    {
      "title": "Ambuja Cements Q2 net profit plunges 90 pc as margins come under pressure",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/quarterly-results/ambuja-cements-q2-net-profit-plunges-90-pc-as-margins-come-under-pressure-126102900887_1.html",
      "description": "Ambuja Cements Ltd reported a 90 per cent year-on-year plunge in consolidated net profit to Rs 236 crore for the September quarter, as higher fuel and logistics costs and seasonal weakness squeezed operating margins at the Adani Group company.\nThe year-earlier profit of Rs 2,336 crore included a Rs 1,697 crore reversal of an income-tax provision, tempering the significance of the reported decline.\nRevenue from operations rose 0.2 per cent to Rs 9,197 crore in the quarter ended September 30, while operating earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation (EBITDA) fell 27.9 per cent to Rs 1,271 crore, the company said in its earnings release.\nCement sales volume declined 0.6 per cent year-on-year to 16.5 million tonnes. EBITDA per tonne fell to Rs 770 from Rs 1,061 a year earlier, while the EBITDA margin contracted to 13.8 per cent from 19.2 per cent.\nAmbuja attributed the pressure to higher petcoke and coal prices, constrained coal availability, and increased diesel and",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-29T10:14:03"
    },
    {
      "title": "SBI Mutual Fund's AUM rises 10% to ₹13.1 trn; H1 operating profit up 11%",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/sbi-mutual-fund-s-aum-rises-10-to-13-1-trn-h1-operating-profit-up-11-126102900707_1.html",
      "description": "SBI Funds Management Ltd, the asset manager of SBI Mutual Fund, reported a 10 per cent year-on-year increase in quarterly average assets under management (QAAUM) to Rs 13.1 lakh crore for the quarter ended September 30, 2026, while operating profit for the first half of the financial year rose 11 per cent to Rs 1,797 crore.\nOperating revenue for the six months increased 12 per cent from a year earlier to Rs 2,336 crore, the company said in a press release.\nActively managed equity assets averaged nearly Rs 9 lakh crore in the September quarter, up 9 per cent year-on-year, giving the company a 12.4 per cent market share in the segment. Assets under management in systematic investment plans (SIPs) rose 15 per cent to Rs 2.07 lakh crore, representing a 12.3 per cent market share.\nThe growth in equity and SIP assets underscores the scale of SBI Funds Management's presence in India's mutual fund industry, particularly in actively managed equity products and systematic investment-led ...",
